title: Math::Min accepts vec3 arguments without a vec3 binding
updated_at: "2026-09-08T19:14:33Z"
---
Reported 2026-09-09. `vec3 a, b; Math::Min(a, b);` should produce a compiler error because Openplanet exposes only scalar Math::Min overloads. Reproduced and fixed in src/typecheck/checker.rs with a red/green regression covering vec2, vec3, vec4, quat rejection and int/float controls. The external overload-set checker now rejects concrete named/object arguments against primitive parameters while retaining neutral handling for unknown/error shapes.